*PPD-Adobe: "4.3"
*% Foilwright -- PPD for ALPS MD-5500 driven through the Microsoft
*% PostScript Printer Driver V3 (DOMAIN.md 3.2 / 7.1, D-001).
*%
*% Copyright (C) 2026 JunkQuality (github.com/KM-KUMA/Foilwright)
*% SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
*%
*% This file is ASCII only on purpose: it is parsed by the Windows print
*% stack, and non-ASCII bytes in a PPD are a portability risk. Rationale
*% and Japanese notes live in docs/DOMAIN.md, not here.
*%
*% Minimal first cut: A4 and 600dpi only. Ink specification method,
*% media type, halftone and the rest of 7.1 are added once this
*% loads and a job reaches the converter (Phase 2).

*FormatVersion: "4.3"
*FileVersion: "0.1"
*LanguageEncoding: ISOLatin1
*LanguageVersion: English
*PCFileName: "FOILWRT.PPD"
*Manufacturer: "JunkQuality"
*Product: "(Foilwright)"
*PSVersion: "(3010.000) 0"
*ModelName: "Foilwright MD-5500"
*ShortNickName: "Foilwright MD-5500"
*NickName: "Foilwright MD-5500"

*LanguageLevel: "3"
*ColorDevice: True
*DefaultColorSpace: RGB
*FileSystem: False
*Throughput: "1"
*TTRasterizer: Type42

*% Page geometry.
*%
*% The paper table (papers/5000-series.yaml) is in dots at 600dpi and
*% describes the *printable* area; PPD wants PostScript points (1/72in)
*% and the *physical* sheet. Conversion is dots * 72 / 600 = dots * 0.12.
*%
*%   sheet     4958 x 7017 dots = 595 x 842 pt
*%   printable 4800 x 6372 dots = 576 x 764.64 pt
*%   left margin  80 dots = 9.6 pt
*%   top margin  284 dots = 34.08 pt  -> bottom margin 361 dots = 43.32 pt
*%
*% ImageableArea is measured from the bottom-left corner, so the lower
*% edge carries the bottom margin, not the top one. Keeping this
*% conversion here is deliberate: mm and points must not travel past the
*% L3 boundary (DOMAIN.md 4.1).

*OpenUI *PageSize: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 10 AnySetup *PageSize
*DefaultPageSize: A4
*PageSize A4/A4: "<</PageSize[595 842]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *PageSize

*OpenUI *PageRegion: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 20 AnySetup *PageRegion
*DefaultPageRegion: A4
*PageRegion A4/A4: "<</PageSize[595 842]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *PageRegion

*DefaultImageableArea: A4
*ImageableArea A4/A4: "9.6 43.32 585.6 807.96"

*DefaultPaperDimension: A4
*PaperDimension A4/A4: "595 842"

*% Resolution. 1200x600 exists on the hardware (profiles/md-5500.yaml)
*% and is declared once the 600dpi path is proven end to end.

*OpenUI *Resolution/Resolution: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 30 AnySetup *Resolution
*DefaultResolution: 600dpi
*Resolution 600dpi/600 dpi: "<</HWResolution[600 600]>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *Resolution

*% Magic colours are matched on exact RGB values, so any colour
*% management between the application and the converter breaks them
*% (DOMAIN.md 6.3, D-021). Declaring the device as plain RGB is the
*% first half of the defence; whether the Windows driver still applies
*% ICM has to be measured in Phase 2.

*DefaultOutputOrder: Normal
*OpenUI *OutputOrder/Output Order: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 40 AnySetup *OutputOrder
*OutputOrder Normal/Normal: ""
*CloseUI: *OutputOrder
